     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dirt = dt.DIRT(target_func, preconditioner, ftt, bridge)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7b8df759",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Debiasing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e490f6cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now, we evaluate the accuracy of the Laplace approximation to the posterior, and the DIRT approximation, by using each to generate proposals for an independence MCMC sampler.\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we consider the Laplace approximation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "ab7eeeb1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Acceptance rate: 0.68.\n",
      "Mean IACT: 2.74.\n",
      "Max IACT: 3.91.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from torch.distributions import MultivariateNormal\n",
    "\n",
    "num_steps = 10_000\n",
    "\n",
    "laplace_approx = MultivariateNormal(bs_map.flatten(), cov_map)\n",
    "samples_laplace = laplace_approx.sample((num_steps,)).to(device)\n",
    "potentials_laplace = -laplace_approx.log_prob(samples_laplace)\n",
    "potentials_true = neglogpost(samples_laplace)\n",
    "\n",
    "res = dt.run_independence_sampler(\n",
    "    samples_laplace, \n",
    "    potentials_laplace, \n",
    "    potentials_true\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Acceptance rate: {res.acceptance_rate:.2f}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean IACT: {res.iacts.mean():.2f}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max IACT: {res.iacts.max():.2f}.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4076122",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "These results suggest that the Laplace approximation is a reasonably good approximation to the posterior on its own.\n",
    "\n",
    "We now repeat the same analysis using the DIRT approximation to the posterior as the proposal density."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "df6709f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Acceptance rate: 0.91.\n",
      "Mean IACT: 1.26.\n",
      "Max IACT: 1.38.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "num_steps = 10_000\n",
    "\n",
    "rs = dirt.reference.random(n=num_steps, d=dirt.dim, device=device)\n",
    "samples_dirt, potentials_dirt = dirt.eval_irt(rs)\n",
    "potentials_true = neglogpost(samples_dirt)\n",
    "\n",
    "res = dt.run_independence_sampler(\n",
    "    samples_dirt, \n",
    "    potentials_dirt, \n",
    "    potentials_true\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Acceptance rate: {res.acceptance_rate:.2f}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean IACT: {res.iacts.mean():.2f}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max IACT: {res.iacts.max():.2f}.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d1f5a6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "These results suggest that the efficiency of the independence sampler improves significantly when the DIRT approximation to the posterior is used as the proposal density (of course, the DIRT density has a significantly greater construction cost than the Laplace approximation, which should also be considered).\n",
    "\n",
    "@fig-samples shows a set of samples from the posterior for the first four model parameters (in particular, note that the posterior is highly concentrated relative to the prior)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "ed85f229",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
